1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born in/near Odessa, moved to St. Petersburg. Successful businessman. Possibly purchaser of Bugatti Type 13 Model while still in St. Petersburg, as an "М.С. Плотников" raced in the 1912 "Варшавском пробеге" as numb
2 CONC er 19. Did not fare well. Left Russia after 1917, settled in Poland, was entrpreneur in paper industry. Name appears frequently in Polish business journals. Lived in Klucze, where he was director of the paper factory, but also had
2 CONC  a villa in Konstancin and a home/office in downtown Warsaw, on Moniuszki street, in the same building in which Pilsudski had lived. Brought driver with him, as well as a passion for Bugattis.
