1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stanislaw Szwarcsztajn won the Rally of Poland in 1927. A passionate car-racer. Co-owner with Maurycy, Ignacz, Adam Szwarcsztajn of paper factories in Klucze and elsewhere.  Later, co-owner with Mihal Plotnikoff of
2 CONC  paper factories. Married Plotnikoff's daughter Natalia around 1930. Promised to give up racing, but couldn't keep the promise and divorced Natalia, returning to race until the war. Had two daughters. After the war, arrived in Rio
2 CONC  de Janeiro, where he was involved in industry. Not known when he died.
